filtered into folders all of my  newsletter services are automatically  filtered into and out of my inbox and  into a folder everything that's  membership related gets filtered into a  separate folder I never see that stuff  in my inbox that is nine  percent of my email right there great  I'm nine-tenths of the way there then  you've got to manually triage okay I go  through email more often than some  people and maybe I don't need to but we  do have things that come up with the  production of the show tech issues might  have to be in touch with affiliates or  sales issues or anything get involved in  like a you know figuring out whether an  advertiser is a good fit for us or not  or something like that so I need to see  if those urgent things come in but those  take under 30 seconds to respond to okay  and what my goal is is I never want to  look at an email more than two times I  look at it the first time can I answer  this email in under 30 seconds if it  even needs a response if the answer is  yes I do it some people say you do your  10 second responses everything else gets  triaged if the email takes more than 30  seconds for me to answer I ask myself  does that this have to be done today or  does this have to be done this week if  it's longer than this week I file it and  put a note in my calendar to revisit it  when it needs to be revisited if it's an  email that needs to be dealt with today  I move it to a folder called today if  it's something that needs to be done  this week I move it to a folder called  this week and then at the end of the day  I'll go to my today folder and one after  the other deal with every email that had  to be answered today I am condensing the  email answering periods of the day  drastically anything that's under 30  seconds that really is of a more urgent  nature even though we could debate  whether it's really that urgent or not  gets answered right away and then I look  at my auto filtered stuff membership  emails those newsletters articles stuff  like that once a day or every other day  or whatever this has cut down 75% on the  time I spend on email that's my  suggestion there are services that can  also help with the stuff there are some  services that will gather similar types  of emails and keep them out of your  inbox until you want them delivered you  might say deliver these at 4:30 p.m. and  then you get them all at once  for example I've not found the need to  use those services but I know people who  have found them useful that is my  approach critique it use whatever of it  might be useful for you reduce the  amount of time you're spending on email  because at listen I want to be spending  time researching stuff for the show  generating value creating  content and when I cut down my email 75%  I'm drastically increasing the amount of  time I can spend on just making the best  possible show we've got a great bonus  show coming up for you today make sure  to sign up at david pakman.com slash  membership or at patreon.com slash david  pakman show i'll speak to you then
 

